WEBVTT

00:01:59.746 --> 00:02:02.121
and actually figure out
how to mimic humans.

00:02:02.371 --> 00:02:06.371
The best way is to observe,
is to actually watch people do things,

00:02:06.413 --> 00:02:08.163
and figure out what are they doing,

00:02:08.204 --> 00:02:10.704
what are their thoughts,
their actions, and emotions.

00:02:10.746 --> 00:02:14.579
And so, part of making robots smarter
is actually trying to mimic humans,

00:02:14.621 --> 00:02:16.746
mimic how we do things,

00:02:16.788 --> 00:02:18.871
so maybe they can do it
a little bit better.

00:02:20.413 --> 00:02:21.996
So, some of the tools are varied.

00:02:22.038 --> 00:02:24.496
I’m classically trained
as an electrical engineer.

00:02:24.538 --> 00:02:28.496
I never thought I'd have to understand
things like child psychology,

00:02:28.538 --> 00:02:30.788
infant development.